---
title: Pickled Jalapeños
description: Jalapeño slices quick-pickled in a lightly sweet vinegar brine, with a whole garlic clove per jar.
tags: [pickles]
course: condiment
icons: [pepper-hot, jar, garlic]
difficulty: easy
source:
  name: Love and Lemons
  url: https://www.loveandlemons.com/pickled-jalapenos/
yield: 2%jars
time: 40m
---

Divide the @jalapeño peppers{10}(thinly sliced) between 2 16-ounce lidded #jars{} and place one of the @garlic cloves{2}(whole, peeled) in each jar.

In a #small saucepan{} over low heat, simmer the @distilled white vinegar{1%cup}, @water{1%cup}, @cane sugar{1/3%cup}, and @sea salt{1%tbsp}, stirring occasionally, until the sugar is dissolved, about ~simmer{5%minutes}.

Pour the brine over the jalapeños. Let cool to room temperature, then cover and chill for at least ~chill{30%minutes}.

> **Storing** — Store in the fridge for up to 2 weeks.
